ts/2874341425","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106324#issuecomment-2874341425","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106324","id":2874341425,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6rUvgx","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-12T22:28:15Z","updated_at":"2025-05-13T00:09:38Z","body":"> Didn't we conclude that this wasn't a good option because per-pixel transparency isn't properly supported on Windows + Nvidia + Vulkan, which is by far our most frequent user setup?\r\n\r\nI can add a small check to see if it's on Window with Vulkan, and then not enable it.\r\n\r\n> I still think it would be preferable to remove popup shadows from the editor theme so this isn't necessary. At least until we can ensure that per-pixel transparency works everywhere and has no significant performance impact.\r\n\r\nIs the performance impact really that severe, considering this version is only for the editor? I feel like having the popups be shadowless makes them look really flat and unpolished.","author_association":"MEMBER"