hubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-20T06:38:40Z","updated_at":"2025-08-20T06:38:40Z","body":"Why not always embed PopupMenus/Panels but keep opening AcceptDialogs in separate windows? What's the value of drawing small things outside of editor window? Blender just draws those inside","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3204396046/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3206347850","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106324#issuecomment-3206347850","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106324","id":3206347850,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_HPxK","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-20T13:28:37Z","updated_at":"2025-08-20T13:30:28Z","body":"We should avoid enabling per-pixel transparency on every editor window, as this has a performance impact even if no transparency is displayed. I recall seeing this on X11 in particular.\r\n\r\n> Why not always embed PopupMenus/Panels but keep opening AcceptDialogs in separate windows? What's the value of drawing small things outside of editor window? Blender just draws those inside\r\n\r\nI agree this is probably the way to go, especially as tooltips and popups are created far more often during an editor session (yet window creation is slow, especially on Windows).\r\n\r\nI'm not sure how difficult it is to make certain node types always embedded though. Right now, the Embed Subwindows Viewport property is \"all or nothing\".","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3206347850/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3206367666","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106324#issuecomment-3206367666","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106324","id":3206367666,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_HUmy","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-20T13:34:14Z","updated_at":"2025-08-20T13:34:14Z","body":"> Why not always embed PopupMenus/Panels but keep opening AcceptDialogs in separate windows? What's the value of drawing small things outside of editor window? Blender just draws those inside\r\n\r\nNative windows are not limited to the parent window bounds, this is pretty much the only benefit (but important one for long menus).\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n  <summary>Example</summary>\r\n\r\n<img width=\"770\" height=\"1218\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-08-20 at 16 30 46\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/51165bd7-7bd7-47be-8761-7a7865d4af7a\" />\r\n\r\n</details>","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3206367666/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3206372706","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106324#issuecomment-3206372706","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106324","id":3206372706,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_HV1i","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-20T13:35:43Z","updated_at":"2025-08-20T13:35:43Z","body":"> Native windows are not limited to the parent window bounds, this is pretty much the only benefit (but important one for long menus).\r\n\r\nCould we do this only for popups that are too large to fit in the window? This way, we only pay the window creation cost when it's really needed.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3206372706/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3206384702","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106324#issuecomment-3206384702","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106324","id":3206384702,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_HYw-","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-20T13:39:13Z","updated_at":"2025-08-20T13:39:13Z","body":"> This way, we only pay the window creation cost when it's really needed.\r\n\r\nOr we might keep a pool of reusable popup windows alive but hidden (there's at most 3-4 menus visible at the same time) instead of creating a new one every time a window is opened (needs testing, I have not checked if there's any performance benefit from this).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3206384702/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3206403046","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106324#issuecomment-3206403046","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106324","id":3206403046,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_HdPm","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-20T13:43:35Z","updated_at":"2025-08-20T13:43:50Z","body":"> Native windows are not limited to the parent window bounds, this is pretty much the only benefit (but important one for long menus).\r\n\r\nIt's the same for tooltips.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"257\" height=\"390\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9ce792f5-3c06-4c33-bddb-6df375a02187\" />\r\n\r\nWhile there is space to fit it inside window here, clamping causes inconsistent tooltip positions.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3206403046/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3206404238","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106324#issuecomment-3206404238","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106324","id":3206404238,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_HdiO","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-20T13:43:54Z","updated_at":"2025-08-25T00:09:54Z","body":"> Native windows are not limited to the parent window bounds, this is pretty much the only benefit (but important one for long menus).\r\n\r\nBlender works around that by implementing scroll, it works with both mousewheel and by hovering on the lower/upper edge of the menu:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"606\" height=\"354\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6bd48091-1e17-440e-b7a4-96f0f22c1296\" /><br>\r\n\r\nI thinks it's a good solution considering the whole situation is an edgecase, and it's useful to have for menus that are too big for the entire screen (not just the window), especially on mobile\r\n\r\n_Edit: just found that godot popup menus already have a scroll container, so they work with mousewheel and draw a scrollbar._","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3206404238/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performe